BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wonder Workshop: Pollution Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T153000
UID:6a07629a43b41b3d0066bfad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you ever think about the impact of one little person or one
  tiny thing on the planet? When one pollutant becomes many\, the planet hu
 rts. But when one person becomes many\, positive change can happen. In thi
 s workshop\, you will design and build your own creature or machine that w
 ill help keep our precious planet clean!\nPlus\, enter a prize draw for a 
 chance to win an awesome book.\nFor kids ages 4 to 8.\nSpace is limited.\n
 Gentle Reminder:\nDue to high demand\, we kindly encourage all participant
 s to arrive on time. Please note that if a participant is more than\n5 min
 utes late\n\, their spot will be forfeited and offered to someone on the w
 aitlist or walk-ins.\nThank you for your understanding and cooperation!\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a07629a43b41b3d0066bfad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
