BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wonder Workshop: Community Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T143000
UID:6a11b7b7490f176f7dd62382@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What do you see when you walk through your community? Have you
  ever thought about building something for your community that would have 
 a positive impact on the people living there? Put on your thinking cap and
  use your imagination to design and build something that would make your c
 ommunity stronger! Plus\, enter a prize draw for a chance to win an awesom
 e book.\nFor kids ages 4 to 8. Space is limited.\nWonder Workshop featured
  title:\nAbuela's Library\nby Lissette Norman\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 
 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a11b7b7490f176f7dd62382
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
