BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yoga Storytime for Toddlers and Pre-Schoolers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T110000
UID:6a15c65d703c3363002a06db@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interactive\, movement-based program where we r
 ead stories and make them come alive with our bodies! Join Megan Snider\, 
 author and Founder of Appleseed Yoga for Kids as she delivers inspiring st
 ories and gets the whole family moving. Class begins and ends with song an
 d breathwork and is filled with pages of creativity and activity. Kids and
  families can sit quietly and listen\, do partial poses or make up their o
 wn\, following our lead. It's ALL yoga! No experience\, mats\, or material
 s required.\nFor toddlers and preschoolers up to age 4 with their caregive
 rs. Older children up to age 8 are invited to register for the session im
 mediately following. Please register all children and adults attending.\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a15c65d703c3363002a06db
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yoga Storytime for Children Ages 4-8
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T111500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T121500
UID:6a15c691f56bd86e00b2284d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interactive\, movement-based program where we r
 ead stories and make them come alive with our bodies! Join Megan Snider\, 
 author and Founder of Appleseed Yoga for Kids as she delivers inspiring st
 ories and gets the whole family moving. Class begins and ends with song an
 d breathwork and is filled with pages of creativity and activity. Kids and
  families can sit quietly and listen\, do partial poses or make up their o
 wn\, following our lead. It's ALL yoga! No experience\, mats\, or material
 s required.\nFor children ages 4-8. Younger children may register for the
  program immediately before. Please register only children.\nInformation C
 ollection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by t
 he Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\
 , 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progr
 am registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library
  handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerli
 ne@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a15c691f56bd86e00b2284d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
