BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wonder Workshop: Community Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T020000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T153000
UID:6a1606c28ea300e26318ae59@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For ages 4 to 8.  Registration opens June 15.\nWhat do you se
 e when you walk through your community? Have you ever thought about buildi
 ng something for your community that would have a positive impact on the p
 eople living there? Put on your thinking cap and use your imagination to d
 esign and build something that would make your community stronger! Plus\, 
 enter a prize draw for a chance to win an awesome book.\nInformation Colle
 ction Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the T
 oronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20
 (c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program r
 egistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library han
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@t
 pl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Lower level program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1606c28ea300e26318ae59
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
